<surname>Tramo</surname><given-names>MJ</given-names></name></person-group><year>1999</year><article-title>Auditory processing in primate cerebral cortex.</article-title><source>Current Opinion in Neurobiology</source><volume>9</volume><fpage>164</fpage><lpage>170</lpage><pub-id pub-id-type="pmid">10322185</pub-id></citation></ref><ref id="pone.0005183-Upadhyay1"><label>15</label><citation citation-type="journal"><person-group person-group-type="author"><name><surname>Upadhyay</surname><given-names>J</given-names></name><name><surname>Ducros</surname><given-names>M</given-names></name><name><surname>Knaus</surname><given-names>TA</given-names></name><name><surname>Lindgren</surname><given-names>KA</given-names></name><name><surname>Silver</surname><given-names>A</given-names></name><etal/></person-group><year>2007</year><article-title>Function and connectivity in human primary auditory cortex: a combined fMRI and DTI study at 3 Tesla.</article-title><source>Cereb Cortex</source><volume>17</volume><fpage>2420</fpage><lpage>2432</lpage><pub-id pub-id-type="pmid">17190967</pub-id></citation></ref><ref id="pone.0005183-Langers2"><label>16</label><citation citation-type="journal"><person-group person-group-type="author"><name><surname>Langers</surname><given-names>DR</given-names></name><name><surname>van Dijk</surname><given-names>P</given-names></name><name><surname>Schoenmaker</surname><given-names>ES</given-names></name><name><surname>Backes</surname><given-names>WH</given-names></name></person-group><year>2007</year><article-title>fMRI activation in relation to sound intensity and loudness.</article-title><source>Neuroimage</source><volume>35</volume><fpage>709</fpage><lpage>718</lpage><pub-id pub-id-type="pmid">17254802</pub-id></citation></ref><ref id="pone.0005183-Bilecen2"><label>17</label><citation citation-type="journal"><person-group person-group-type="author"><name><surname>Bilecen</surname><given-names>D</given-names></name><name><surname>Scheffler</surname><given-names>K</given-names></name><name><surname>Schmid</surname><given-names>N</given-names></name><name><surname>Tschopp</surname><given-names>K</given-names></name><name><surname>Seelig</surname><given-names>J</given-names></name></person-group><year>1998</year><article-title>Tonotopic organization of the human auditory cortex as detected by BOLD-FMRI.</article-title><source>Hear Res</source><volume>126</volume><fpage>19</fpage><lpage>27</lpage><pub-id pub-id-type="pmid">9872130</pub-id></citation></ref><ref id="pone.0005183-Sigalovsky1"><label>18</label><citation citation-type="journal"><person-group person-group-type="author"><name><surname>Sigalovsky</surname><given-names>IS</given-names></name><name><surname>Fischl</surname><given-names>B</given-names></name><name><surname>Melcher</surname><given-names>JR</given-names></name></person-group><year>2006</year><article-title>Mapping an intrinsic MR property of gray matter in auditory cortex of living humans: a possible marker for primary cortex and hemispheric differences.</article-title><source>Neuroimage</source><volume>32</volume><fpage>1524</fpage><lpage>1537</lpage><pub-id pub-id-type="pmid">16806989</pub-id></citation></ref><ref id="pone.0005183-DorsaintPierre1"><label>19</label><citation citation-type="journal"><person-group person-group-type="author"><name><surname>Dorsaint-Pierre</surname><given-names>R</given-names></name><name><surname>Penhune</surname><given-names>VB</given-names></name><name><surname>Watkins</surname><given-names>KE</given-names></name><name><surname>Neelin</surname><given-names>P</given-names></name><name><surname>Lerch</surname><given-names>JP</given-names></name><etal/></person-group><year>2006</year><article-title>Asymmetries of the planum temporale and Heschl's gyrus: relationship to language lateralization.</article-title><source>Brain</source><volume>129</volume><fpage>1164</fpage><lpage>1176</lpage><pub-id pub-id-type="pmid">16537567</pub-id></citation></ref><ref id="pone.0